        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_988280125.1",
        "comments": "This project provides (pseudo-)haplotype two of the diploid genome assembly of the saith, Pollachius virens with a sample provided by Sissel Jentoft. The data generation and assembly were carried out by EBP-Nor (https://www.ebpnor.org/). The fPolVir2.1 assembly is based on 75x PromethION R10 Oxford Nanopore and 62x Arima Hi-C data. The HiFi reads were assembled with hifiasm along with Hi-C data to generate a pair of haplotype-resolved assemblies. K-mers from the two assemblies were used to filter Hi-C reads to create two sets of reads for scaffolding the assemblies (i.e., reads used to scaffold hap1 did not contain k-mers unique to hap2). YaHS was used for scaffolding. FCS-adaptor was used to remove putative adapters, and putative contaminants were removed with FCS-GX. The chromosomes have been ordered and oriented according to fPolPol2.",
